1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,170
Your hyaluronic acid serum and a dermal

2
00:00:02,270 --> 00:00:04,120
filler share one name.

3
00:00:04,220 --> 00:00:06,600
So why can't one do the other's job?

4
00:00:06,600 --> 00:00:09,740
A hyaluronic acid serum cannot do what a

5
00:00:09,740 --> 00:00:11,580
dermal filler does.

6
00:00:11,680 --> 00:00:13,750
Because hyaluronic acid isn't one thing,

7
00:00:13,850 --> 00:00:14,560
it's three.

8
00:00:14,660 --> 00:00:16,640
The kind your body already makes.

9
00:00:16,740 --> 00:00:18,480
The kind in your serum.

10
00:00:18,620 --> 00:00:20,560
The kind a doctor injects.

11
00:00:20,660 --> 00:00:22,560
And the mix-up is an expensive one.

12
00:00:22,660 --> 00:00:24,730
People buy a serum expecting the results

13
00:00:24,830 --> 00:00:25,920
of an injection.

14
00:00:25,920 --> 00:00:28,500
A serum is not filler in a bottle.

15
00:00:28,740 --> 00:00:31,230
The name goes back to 1934 when it was

16
00:00:31,230 --> 00:00:33,310
isolated from the clear jelly inside a

17
00:00:33,310 --> 00:00:34,060
cow's eye.

18
00:00:34,180 --> 00:00:35,130
Remember that?

19
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:36,920
It comes back.

20
00:00:37,020 --> 00:00:38,540
Your body already makes its own.

21
00:00:38,700 --> 00:00:40,770
Most of it sits in your skin, holding

22
00:00:40,770 --> 00:00:41,360
water.

23
00:00:41,360 --> 00:00:43,200
It also lubricates your joints, and it's

24
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:45,500
still doing its job inside your eye.

25
00:00:45,600 --> 00:00:47,240
Here's where the two versions really

26
00:00:47,240 --> 00:00:47,670
split.

27
00:00:47,670 --> 00:00:49,770
A serum's version stays mostly at the

28
00:00:49,770 --> 00:00:51,800
surface, supporting hydration.

29
00:00:51,800 --> 00:00:53,850
A filler's version is completely different

30
00:00:53,850 --> 00:00:54,560
chemistry.

31
00:00:54,660 --> 00:00:56,720
It's cross-linked into a gel and placed

32
00:00:56,720 --> 00:00:59,230
beneath the skin, where it can physically

33
00:00:59,230 --> 00:01:00,010
add volume.

34
00:01:00,180 --> 00:01:02,250
In a serum, size decides almost

35
00:01:02,350 --> 00:01:03,480
everything.

36
00:01:03,580 --> 00:01:06,440
Large chains mostly stay near the surface,

37
00:01:06,540 --> 00:01:09,200
forming a hydrating film.

38
00:01:09,290 --> 00:01:11,370
Smaller ones may travel farther into the

39
00:01:11,470 --> 00:01:13,280
upper layers of skin.

40
00:01:13,380 --> 00:01:15,450
Neither one behaves like an injectable

41
00:01:15,450 --> 00:01:16,080
filler.

42
00:01:16,180 --> 00:01:18,250
So why does the bottle say plumping?

43
00:01:18,400 --> 00:01:20,120
Because hydrated surface cells can

44
00:01:20,120 --> 00:01:22,970
temporarily make fine lines appear softer,

45
00:01:22,970 --> 00:01:26,090
like watering a tired houseplant, not like

46
00:01:26,090 --> 00:01:27,600
adding a new branch.

47
00:01:27,860 --> 00:01:28,720
And here's the part.

48
00:01:28,820 --> 00:01:30,440
The marketing skips.

49
00:01:30,540 --> 00:01:33,020
Hyaluronic acid binds water and holds onto

50
00:01:33,180 --> 00:01:33,460
it.

51
00:01:33,660 --> 00:01:35,730
It does not manufacture water out of

52
00:01:35,830 --> 00:01:36,580
nothing.

53
00:01:36,700 --> 00:01:38,410
Skip that step, and you're hiring a

54
00:01:38,410 --> 00:01:40,540
lifeguard for an empty swimming pool.

55
00:01:40,540 --> 00:01:42,220
A filler is chemically different.

56
00:01:42,380 --> 00:01:44,450
Its chains are cross-linked into a stable,

57
00:01:44,550 --> 00:01:46,820
connected grid that holds its own shape

58
00:01:46,820 --> 00:01:49,160
once it's placed beneath the skin.

59
00:01:49,260 --> 00:01:51,960
Is a filler just serum with a needle?

60
00:01:52,050 --> 00:01:53,600
Not even close.

61
00:01:53,740 --> 00:01:56,230
That's worth putting in very large

62
00:01:56,380 --> 00:01:57,190
letters.

63
00:01:57,300 --> 00:01:59,240
Do not inject yourself.

64
00:01:59,340 --> 00:02:03,360
That's the FDA's own wording, not ours.

65
00:02:03,460 --> 00:02:05,680
Dermal fillers are a medical procedure

66
00:02:05,680 --> 00:02:08,860
with real risks, including tissue death,

67
00:02:08,860 --> 00:02:10,750
vision loss, and stroke.

68
00:02:10,860 --> 00:02:14,010
Choose a provider trained to perform the

69
00:02:14,010 --> 00:02:15,100
injection.

70
00:02:15,300 --> 00:02:16,720
Same ingredient family.

71
00:02:16,820 --> 00:02:18,340
Different size, different structure,

72
00:02:18,360 --> 00:02:19,720
different location.

73
00:02:19,820 --> 00:02:22,600
So a different result.

74
00:02:22,690 --> 00:02:25,640
The body's version is a resident.

75
00:02:25,740 --> 00:02:28,880
The serum's version is a moisturizer.

76
00:02:28,980 --> 00:02:31,360
The filler's version is a construction

77
00:02:31,360 --> 00:02:32,160
project.

78
00:02:32,260 --> 00:02:34,160
So buy the serum for hydration.

79
00:02:34,260 --> 00:02:35,720
It does that job well.

80
00:02:35,810 --> 00:02:38,200
Just don't buy it expecting volume.

81
00:02:38,300 --> 00:02:39,250
Serum hydrates.

82
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:40,960
Filler adds volume.

83
00:02:41,100 --> 00:02:42,760
Same name, different jobs.

84
00:02:42,860 --> 00:02:46,280
And yes, the cow's eye came back.
